    dict(key='06-act-2', kind='console', title='Act Two — The same recursion, three types',
         body='TWO. The same recursion, three types.\n  <Integer> traverse: [21, 23, 19, 25, 24, 22, 20], depth 7\n  <String>  traverse: [Mon, Tue, Wed, Thu, Fri, Sat, Sun], depth 7\n  <Reading> traverse: [Mon 21 C, ... Sun 20 C], depth 7\n  linearSearch(new String("Fri")) = index 4 at depth 5: equals compares the text, == would not match',
         narration='The same recursion works for every type. [[slnc 400]] Traversal of the temperatures, the day names, and the readings. [[slnc 300]] Each one goes seven calls deep. [[slnc 500]] And a search for a new string, Fri, finds it at index four, five calls deep. [[slnc 400]] It works because the search asks equals, which compares the text, not the object.'),
